From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Johansson <1911831+djohansson@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fix missing cstdlib include

phmap_base.h calls std::abort() (via PHMAP_THROW_IMPL/PHMAP_THROW_IMPL_MSG
when exceptions are disabled) without including <cstdlib>, relying on it
being pulled in transitively (e.g. via MSVC STL's <string>/<memory>).
Building against libc++ instead of MSVC STL no longer pulls it in
transitively, so std::abort is undeclared:
  error: no member named 'abort' in namespace 'std'; did you mean simply 'abort'?
---
 parallel_hashmap/phmap_base.h | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/parallel_hashmap/phmap_base.h b/parallel_hashmap/phmap_base.h
index 0000000..0000000 100644
--- a/parallel_hashmap/phmap_base.h
+++ b/parallel_hashmap/phmap_base.h
@@ -36,6 +36,7 @@
 
 #include <algorithm>
 #include <cassert>
+#include <cstdlib>
 #include <cstddef>
 #include <initializer_list>
 #include <iterator>
-- 
